# Upstream paths this workspace deliberately does NOT vendor.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `verify-vendored-llama-cpp.sh` used to walk the
# vendored tree and compare each file to upstream. That direction catches an
# EDIT and is blind to an OMISSION — "a file present upstream but not here is
# expected and is not reported" was the rule, and it made every missing file
# invisible.
#
# It let a real one through. The 2026-08-26 fast-forward to 035e22731a moved
# the Metal shaders to a per-kernel `kernels/*.metal` layout. The vendoring
# step copies files that already exist, so 20 NEW upstream files were never
# taken, and the old single-file `ggml-metal.metal` was deleted as "stale and
# inert" on the strength of a grep for .cpp references — which cannot see a
# CMakeLists that reads `kernels/${kind}.metal`. The verifier reported
# "1764 files: 1764 identical, 0 differing" and the macOS build could not
# configure: `file STRINGS file .../kernels/fa.metal cannot be read`. Linux
# builds with GGML_METAL=OFF and never noticed, which is why it landed green.
#
# So the check now runs BOTH directions, and this file is what makes the
# reverse direction expressible: everything upstream ships inside a directory
# we vendor from must either be present or be named here. Anything else is a
# failure, not a shrug.
#
# One glob per line, matched against the upstream-relative path with `case`.
# `#` comments and blank lines ignored. Keep it as tight as the truth allows:
# a pattern that is broader than the intent is how the next omission hides.

